By taking the sum of all glance durations for each task, we obtain the total glance time (TGT) per task. The distribution for this measure is show in Fig. 5 with extreme outliers removed; these were identified based on the inter-quartile range method described by Tukey [33] and defined as occurring outside the range Q 2 ± 3 ( Q 3 - Q 1 ) where Q 2 is the median of the data set and Q 1 and Q 3 the 25th and 75th percentiles. Twenty data points were removed, corresponding to 1.06% of the data. Outlying data points occur when the participant fails to successfully complete the touchscreen task and reverts their attention to the forward roadway, requiring a second attempt to complete the task.

