The mean TGT per task is 2.54 s while the median is 2.36 s, indicating positive skew of the distribution. The expected TGT range for this array size given by Irune and Burnett [27] of 2–3.5 s encompasses 50% of the data, from the 35th to 85th percentile.

Two-way within-subjects ANOVA analysis of mean TGT per task ( Fig. 6 ) indicated a significant interaction between visual and haptic feedback ( F (2, 68) = 6.177, p  < 0.005). Mean TGT was reduced when haptic feedback was present; simple main effects analysis showed a statistically significant reduction from 2.76 s to 2.32 s for the ‘delayed’ visual feedback condition ( F (1, 34) = 23.514, p  < 0.001), and from 2.96 s to 2.40 s for the ‘none’ condition ( F (1, 34) = 40.329, p  < 0.001).

