The additional subjective measures included in the follow-up questionnaire provided further evidence of user acceptance of the haptic touchscreen technology. For the forced-choice ‘Most preferred’ question, 32 of the 36 participants (89%) chose visual + haptic feedback as most preferred. Furthermore, subjects ‘agreed’ overall that haptic feedback made the touchscreen both easier and more pleasurable to use (Likert scale means of 4.2 and 4.1 respectively, see Fig. 12 ). Subjects agreed less strongly (mean = 3.7) that touchscreen haptic feedback should feel like mechanical push switches.

